WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.440
Plus, sometimes I just feel like going out and having something nice to eat.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.070
Aren't we a bit too busy for that right now?

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.120
I feel horrible just going between school and home.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.120
What do you want to eat, anyway?

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.250
Italian...

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.000
Or maybe Italian!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.250
Can't you just go to a diner?

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.030
I don't mean like that.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.260
I want to go to the kind of place where they write the menu in Italian on the tablecloth.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.010
I know what you mean, but tomorrow's going to be busy too.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.160
We should get some sleep.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.520
You're right, but let's keep going a little longer.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.020
So anyway...

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.030
One!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.870
Two!

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.130
Three!

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.150
Four!

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.170
Five!

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.020
Six.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.160
Hiro?

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.720
What's up, Hiro?

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.330
I just woke up.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.830
You look pretty sleepy.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.960
I'm amazed you're up this early.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:11.920
Yeah.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.050
Um, want to join in?

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.930
Maybe I will. Hold on a second.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:25.310
July 12th

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:25.310
"Three Stars x Lycopene"

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.290
One!

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:26.990
Two!

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.200
Three!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.030
Four.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:29.960
Five!

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:30.600
Six!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.150
It's hot out.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.240
But this felt better than I expected. It woke me right up.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.620
Why don't we do it every day?

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.120
If you can wake up early enough, that is.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.200
Yeah, if I can wake up that early.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.330
What are you guys doing today?

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.990
Let's pick tomatoes!

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.330
It's tomato weather!

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.090
Freshly picked tomatoes are delicous!

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.800
If we don't pick them today, they'll get too ripe.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.180
Yeah, it's about time to harvest them.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.750
Let's all make something with them once they're picked.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.890
That sounds fun!

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.440
Let me go get my phone, then.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.190
Your phone?

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.690
Um, well, I thought I'd take pictures.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:19.820
Me too.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.780
I'll take some too.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.570
I'll get my sketchbook!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.750
These are about ripe, aren't they?

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.960
One, two, three...

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.460
Look at all the tomatoes!

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.850
Miya and tomatoes.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.930
They really grew well, didn't they?

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.600
Yeah, everyone worked hard on them.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.100
We made props and tied them up with string.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:57.440
Yeah. Nori got mad when I tied them all up tight.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:02.110
I wasn't mad! I just read that the stalks get bigger as they grow.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.840
That was around when we saw the first few green tomatoes, right?

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.890
Yeah. They were so cute.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.620
I'm amazed they got this big.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.000
There'll be plenty more too!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.970
Tomatoes are pretty hard to get off the vine.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.680
Is this the right way to pick them?

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.350
Press your finger right at the stem. They come off easy if you twist.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.350
You're right!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.700
The harvest is finished!

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.300
Two, four, six, eight... Thirty-six.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.190
We sure picked a lot.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.940
They're such a pretty color.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.950
Then, esteemed gentlemen, let us commence the Tomato Summit immediately!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.490
Tomato Summit?

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.490
It's where we discuss the fate of the tomatoes!

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.290
The fate of the tomatoes?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.500
Why don't we talk it over at my place?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.880
Sure!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.130
Oh, there's the landlady.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.130
Yo.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.130
I'm here about the new recycling days.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.890
Good morning!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.310
Did you just pick those tomatoes? They look great.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.890
Yeah, thanks for the idea.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.630
Good work.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.960
Tomatoes have a lot of lycopene and stuff.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.570
They're great for your figure, and they taste great raw or cooked.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:25.900
We're going to cook these. Would you like to come over and have some later?

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.350
Really?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.280
I'll pick up something on my way over, then.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.290
You don't have to worry about it.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.090
I don't know how long we're going to take, so I'll give you a call later.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:36.790
Sure thing.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:39.790
Tomato!

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.300
Tomato, tomato!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.670
Tomato!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.970
Here, I thought we'd sample them.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.340
Yay!

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.180
They're tasty!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.890
The flavor's so intense!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.230
They're sweet!

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.980
Nice and tangy too.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.310
Yeah.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.940
I wonder what the best thing to make would be.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:03.820
I know!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:08.070
Tomato spaghetti! Tomato pizza! Tomato rice! Tomato-don!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.490
That's a bit much.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.910
If we make tomato sauce, we can use it for pasta and pizza.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:17.290
How about an Insalata Caprese?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.520
What's that, Nori?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.710
Caprese?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.830
Wait, you don't know?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.470
I thought it was the most popular salad in Italy.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.340
What else goes in it?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.850
Mozzarella cheese and basil.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.350
Oh, that!

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.310
Well, Signor Yuno, that's not in my dictionary.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.440
Then we need basil and mozzarella cheese.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.170
Who's going to run and get them?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.360
Mart

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.360
Open 9AM

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:55.740
Mozzarella cheese, laurier, olive oil...

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.960
The cart is full of European languages!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.420
I don't think I've ever used olive oil.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.580
I probably have some at home.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.670
It's great on bread instead of butter.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.680
Nori, were you born in Italy?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.970
Oh, Yuno, Nori, and Nazuna!

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.840
Miss Yoshinoya?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.980
Hello!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.100
Hi, everyone. Are you all shopping together?

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.180
Yeah.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.150
I've got to go back to school and keeping working after this.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.080
You have to finish grading the exams?

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.990
It must be tough.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:36.990
It is, but I get to see how hard you all worked, so I have to keep going.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.500
Thanks for grading them.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.870
Thank you.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.870
Thanks, everyone.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.460
Miss Yoshinoya seemed tired.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:53.970
While we've got time off after exams, the teachers have to work hard grading them.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.180
Bikes/Pedestrians

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.180
Only

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.640
I wonder how I did on the test.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.140
Nazuna, why are you so worried?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.160
We studied together, right?

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:04.730
You'll be fine.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:10.240
I'm still worried about my English and Math, though.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.990
I'm more worried about art history.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.870
Let's hurry back.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.030
Okay!

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.040
Bikes/Pedestrians

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.040
Only

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:29.880
Hey Sae, about how many hours a day do you spend working?

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.540
It varies from day to day.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.300
Sometimes I can't get anything done even when I'm sitting at my desk.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.810
You're so tense when that happens.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.680
Sorry, I try not to be. I guess it doesn't work, though.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.690
Yeah, I just try not to bother you too much then.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.680
Sorry! Don't worry about it!

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.070
Anyway, changing the subject, there are also times when everything goes smoothly.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.860
Must be tough.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.570
Miyako, what do you do in your room?

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.080
Like when you're not working on anything.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.370
Nothin'.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.540
Nothing?

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.420
I have fun not doing anything.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.550
Miya must have drawn this.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.550
Hidamari

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.550
Ristorante Hidamari?

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.520
Ristorante?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.910
That's Italian for "restaurant."

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.060
They must have decided to name it.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.140
We're back!

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.060
Welcome back!

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:26.900
Sorry we took so long.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.060
Thanks.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:32.570
I know you just got back, but I'm going to put you to work again.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.710
Okay.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.270
Just say the word.

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:37.280
I'll go get my apron.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.780
I'll go write that we're preparing.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.660
Wouldn't want the customers getting confused and wandering in early.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.160
Have you already decided on a menu?

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.790
I'm still wondering about dessert.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.710
Can you think of any desserts that use tomatoes?

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.220
Why don't I look something up online?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.220
Okay. Can you handle dessert, then?

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:59.050
No problem.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.820
Can I help too?

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.060
Sure, thanks.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:06.330
Sae, can you make the tomato sauce?

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.690
Will do.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:10.230
I'll take the ingredients and make it at my place.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.610
Thanks.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.530
There we go.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.030
That was fast!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.370
The internet is great for things like this.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.870
Memopad

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.700
You can do anything, can't you?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.460
Not really.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.210
Why don't you give the computer a try?

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.310
It seems tough.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:31.290
It isn't really.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.880
You might find you're good at it if you give it a try.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.130
I'll help you out anytime.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.880
Okay, thanks.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:44.180
We're working on it in three different rooms.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.310
The kitchen in here really isn't big enough.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.190
It's great that everyone's helping out.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:58.360
It's from Nori.
They've started on the dessert.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:00.740
What are they making?

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.150
She says it's a secret.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.710
Chopping is fun!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:16.710
Let's see... Saute the garlic and onion, then add the sliced tomatoes...

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:21.050
Miyako, isn't that enough? You're making me cry.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.430
You should wear goggles too.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.060
It's too late for that!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.510
All right, chopping complete!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.560
Miyako...

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.690
All right, the soup's done!

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:49.280
Grading these tests is really wearing me down.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.080
I want to go eat something tasty.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Miss Kuwahara

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Keep at it.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Kuwahara

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.670
Keep at it.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.680
Miss Yoshinoya

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.680
Now that I think of it, doesn't grading
sound kind of like revolving?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.680
Yoshinoya

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.680
Now that I think it, doesn't grading [saiten]
sound kind of like revolving? [kaiten]

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.680
Yeah, sure.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.020
Miss Kuwahara

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.020
Don't get stuck in a
loop of bad puns.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.020
Kuwahara

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.020
Don't get stuck in a loop of bad puns.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.310
Miss Yoshinoya? Is something wrong?

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.150
It's nothing.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.530
You're working hard.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.860
At this rate, you'll be done today.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.200
It's no good! I can't get around to it!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.290
Is there something wrong with Miss Yoshinoya?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.540
I'm not sure.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.010
I'm hungry.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.760
Hold on, Miya!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.260
The longer we wait, the better it'll taste.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.890
It'll only take a little longer.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:50.390
Sorry to make you season it, Hiro.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:54.200
Don't worry. Even doing this much is a great help.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:55.230
Thanks, Sae.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:59.270
But you're always cooking for me, so sometimes...

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.530
Hiro, what about me?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.630
Thanks, Miya.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:06.360
Eat as hard as you worked.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.420
It's not like you have to tell her. She will anyway.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.710
It's done!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:20.300
I really wanted some yakisoba the other night.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:24.820
I couldn't decide whether to have some cup noodles.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.800
Yeah, I've had that happen.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:31.140
But I got so involved in chatting that I fell asleep.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.770
Is that chilled enough?

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.520
No, not quite.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.860
Inbox

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.860
Hiro

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.860
Announcement

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.860
Everyone come on over!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:51.410
Sorry we're late. Can we put the dessert in the fridge?

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:53.910
Go right ahead.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.380
Tasty!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:03.960
To make Caprese,

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:09.180
you layer the tomato, the mozzarella cheese, and the basil like this.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:12.970
The red of the tomato looks pretty on the green of the basil.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.770
These are the colors of the Italian flag.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.480
Red, green, and white.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:19.810
You're right.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.030
Hiro, have you called the landlady?

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.030
No Smoking

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.210
Hi?

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.390
This is Hiro.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:40.160
We're finally done. Sorry it took so long.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.920
So, what did you make?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.800
You guys go ahead and start.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.930
I'll be over in a little bit. Later.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.780
Let's go.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.150
It's done.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.980
What a feast!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.700
Let's eat!

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:00.850
Wait, Miya!

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:02.690
Let's take pictures to remember this.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.190
Let's eat!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.030
It's so good, I could cry.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.740
We were really hungry.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:17.790
Hiro, you sure made a lot.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:23.420
I'm impressed by how well you can all cook.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.920
That's Hiro for ya.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.920
Not just me. Everyone helped out.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.930
We really managed to make a full course dinner of tomatoes.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:35.720
It's enough to make a tomato-hater cry.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.270
It's probably too late to ask, but you all like tomatoes, right?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.600
I love 'em.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:42.560
Me too.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.070
Yeah! I love them!

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.900
Miya, are there any foods you don't like?

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.410
I can't think of any.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.160
It really is a great day for tomatoes.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.500
I've been thinking about them every day since we planted them.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.040
I did notice you paying a lot of attention to them.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.800
Yeah. I've talked to them, and lent them my umbrella.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:08.920
Your umbrella?

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:14.640
Yeah. After they turn red, they can split if they're rained on.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.160
Oh, that was you?

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.980
I was wondering why someone put umbrellas up over tomatoes.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.190
You treated them like your children.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.190
You sure were worth your salt.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.460
Yeah, tomatoes are good with just salt.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.200
Hello?

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.700
Hey, I brought a present.

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.450
Though it's just some sweets from the store.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.910
Thanks. Come right in.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.460
All right, thanks.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.550
Hey there.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.800
Hello.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.710
Wow, look at it all!

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.220
You guys made all this by yourselves?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.720
Yeah, everyone helped out.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:02.230
Man, I really should've brought some wine.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.810
Now for the dolce, made special by us first years!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.610
Tomato sherbet!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.980
Tomato sherbet?

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.900
Let's see...

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.900
This is wonderful.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.490
It came out really well.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.430
Yeah. Nazuna helped out.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:22.090
It was so easy.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:25.250
I'm amazed you guys put so much work in.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.590
I'm sorry.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:30.380
Don't worry about it.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.000
You guys get along really well.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.260
That's great.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.630
Well, we are the same age.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.800
So, how do you like living alone?

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.180
I'm doing my best.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.390
Man, this is great.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.440
I'm not that good at cooking yet, though.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.810
Everyone's like that at first.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:50.820
How about you, Nazuna?

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.320
Sometimes I have dinner with Nori.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.200
It's great that you're getting along and have things to talk about.

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.450
They seem kind of tense.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.120
It's like a surprise interview.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.250
Look at her fuss over them.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.290
Amazing, isn't it?

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:13.180
You guys had better keep learning from the older girls.

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:13.800
Okay.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.800
Keep learning how to cook?

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:19.300
This hurts to listen to.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.640
Thanks, that was really great.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.080
Come back anytime.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.670
Thanks. See you later!

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:33.650
Goodbye!

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.320
Oh, you're all out here?

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:41.990
Miss Yoshinoya?

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:48.580
Here, you can make pasta with this tomato sauce.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.670
Thanks!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.210
Did you make this yourself, Hiro?

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:55.580
No, Sae made it.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:57.970
But Hiro seasoned it.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:02.350
I get it. You all worked on it, right?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.430
Yeah!

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.490
Thank you!

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:12.500
Just seeing you all cheered me up.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.440
See you at school, okay?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.410
Goodbye!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.950
Goodbye, teacher!

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.120
That was fun.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.870
I'm stuffed.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.040
We'll sleep well tonight.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.250
Wasn't that so much fun?

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:29.870
Yeah.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.120
Right!

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:35.770
I hate to break up the party, but isn't it about time to go home?

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:40.890
All right, as of today, Ristorante Hidamari is closed.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.550
Any regrets?

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.890
I wish every day was a tomato day.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.230
That would be terrible for our weight.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.310
Isn't it fine to keep it seasonal?

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.400
Yeah.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:55.610
Um...

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.940
What is it?

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.480
Is there anything else?

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:04.240
I want to remember today's menu, not just have pictures.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.700
Why not come over to my place and use my computer?

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.250
We can save the recipes and pictures in it.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:10.870
Okay!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:15.290
Okay, I'll go get the sign!

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.400
Yunocchi, what's taking so long?

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:30.100
Oh, Miya.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.540
What are you looking at?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.480
That star's so pretty.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.360
Everyone should see it!

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.860
Hey, guys!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.190
The first star!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.700
That's the evening star.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.210
It's pretty.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.710
Isn't it?

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:02.220
Tomorrow will be sunny too.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.720
Yeah!

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.390
I feel so happy for some reason.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:20.070
Good food and great conversation...

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:26.490
Being able to smile every day with my friends...

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:29.450
Hidamari Apartments is such a wonderful place.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.750
I wonder what tomorrow will be like.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
July 12th

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
The end

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
To be
continued
